{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>After he had sent her away.</b> Since Scripture mentioned (Exodus 4:20), \"And Moses took his wife and his sons and set them on a donkey, and he returned to the land of Egypt,\" it was necessary to state here that she was in her father's house, for Moses had sent her there. It is also possible that it means Yithro took her in order to return her to him, even though he had sent her away from himself, because he heard all that Elohim had done for Moses — for from now on it is fitting to go after the king in all wherever he goes."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:17:07.023639062Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}